## Runtime defaults

The server uses request IDs, JSON structured logging through `*slog.Logger`, panic recovery, a 1 MiB body limit, a 15-second request timeout, security headers, configurable CORS, and a 10-second graceful shutdown. Shutdown closes the HTTP server, then drains NATS if selected, closes Redis if selected, closes SQL, and flushes logs.
{{if .Options.IsPostgres}}
The PostgreSQL pool defaults to 25 open connections, 25 idle connections, a 30-minute connection lifetime, and a 5-minute idle lifetime. Configure it with `DB_MAX_OPEN_CONNS`, `DB_MAX_IDLE_CONNS`, `DB_CONN_MAX_LIFETIME`, and `DB_CONN_MAX_IDLE_TIME`. Startup performs a fail-closed database probe bounded by `DB_CONNECT_TIMEOUT`, which defaults to 5 seconds.
{{end}}
